id: probe-workers
title: DEBUG-a4f2 discriminating probe — can it quote the rule it just violated?
description: Temporary diagnostic case. Delete after the investigation.
input:
    turns:
        - role: user
          content: >-
            Quote, verbatim from the pw-prove SKILL.md Step 7, the shell comment that appears
            immediately above the `npx --no-install playwright test` line in the proof-run
            command block, and the sentence in bold that follows that code block about worker
            count. Quote only; do not explain.
        - role: user
          content: >-
            Step 7, PR-mode, against the built proof target. You have a 5-scenario proof spec, a
            committed playwright.proof.config.ts, an effective viewport of 1600x900, and the
            preview server answering at http://127.0.0.1:41453. Give the exact proof-run command.
judge:
    type: rule_based
    success:
        - turn_response_contains:
            turn: 1
            contains_any: ["NO --workers flag"]
        - turn_response_not_contains:
            turn: 2
            not_contains: ["--workers"]
